{"duration_api_ms":115689,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"64e66ef7-479a-4cdc-9778-ed2b5396b80c","total_cost_usd":0.5668852,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32335,"cache_read_input_tokens":460326,"output_tokens":10801,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3276},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":42614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1507},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":10801,"cacheReadInputTokens":460326,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32335,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5668852,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3276,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCTMpCLikFC8QZjZCUEi4d","tool_input":{"command":"for f in derived/cost-fix-claude.log derived/craigslist-rerun.log; do echo \"== $f\"; tail -n 8 \"$f\"; done; echo; cut -d, -f1-12 artifacts/kafe_results_to_reproduce.csv","description":"Show log tails and CSV timing columns"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014uwWNrHkAZBp7iS1ntu1ns","tool_input":{"command":"uv run --offline --no-sync python -B -c \"\nimport json,csv,statistics as st\nnames=set(json.load(open('derived/kafe_matrix_summary.json'))['subject_names'])\nrows=[r for r in csv.DictReader(open('artifacts/kafe_results_to_reproduce.csv')) if r['Subject'].strip()]\nrows.sort(key=lambda r:float(r['Detection']))\nprev=0; prevl=0; inc={}; incl={}\nfor r in rows:\n  d=float(r['Detection']); l=float(r['Localization']); inc[r['Subject']]=d-prev; incl[r['Subject']]=l-prevl; prev=d; prevl=l\nprint('run order (by cumulative value):',[r['Subject'] for r in rows][-5:])\nprint('last Detection value', prev, 'sum of Detection column', sum(float(r['Detection']) for r in rows))\nfor lab,rs in [('all60',rows),('scored',[r for r in rows if r['Subject'] in names])]:\n  pb=[inc[r['Subject']]/float(r['Size of All Visible Ctrl Nodes']) for r in rs]\n  ps=[inc[r['Subject']] for r in rs]\n  print(lab,len(rs),'per-subject increment median',st.median(ps),'mean',round(st.mean(ps),1),'max',max(ps),'| per ctrl median',round(st.median(pb),2),'max',round(max(pb),2),'pooled',round(sum(ps)/sum(float(r['Size of All Visible Ctrl Nodes']) for r in rs),2))\n# correlation check: increment vs ctrl nodes vs raw Detection vs ctrl\nimport math\ndef corr(a,b):\n  ma,mb=st.mean(a),st.mean(b); return sum((x-ma)*(y-mb) for x,y in zip(a,b))/math.sqrt(sum((x-ma)**2 for x in a)*sum((y-mb)**2 for y in b))\nc=[float(r['Size of All Visible Ctrl Nodes']) for r in rows]; n=[float(r['Size of All Nodes']) for r in rows]\nprint('corr(increment, ctrl)',round(corr([inc[r['Subject']] for r in rows],c),2),'corr(increment, all nodes)',round(corr([inc[r['Subject']] for r in rows],n),2))\nprint('corr(raw Detection, ctrl)',round(corr([float(r['Detection']) for r in rows],c),2),'corr(raw Detection, rank)',round(corr([float(r['Detection']) for r in rows],list(range(60))),3))\nprint('biggest increments:',sorted(((v,k) for k,v in inc.items()),reverse=True)[:5])\n\"","description":"Test cumulative-counter hypothesis for Detection column"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I stopped before editing anything. One of the brief's premises looks wrong, and the brief says to stop and report in that case.\n\n**Recompute (done):** my figures match the manager's table exactly.\n\n| KAFE ms per visible control | All 60 (median / pooled) | Scored 39 (median / pooled) | Under 300 ms (60 / 39) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Detection only | 25.8 / 20.0 | 35.8 / **25.7** | 60 of 60 / 39 of 39 |\n| CrawlKnfg + CrawlPcnfg | 3,823.9 / 3,117.8 | 4,333.2 / 3,601.0 | 0 of 60 / 0 of 39 |\n| All seven phases | 22,683.3 / 23,000.8 | 28,370.8 / 23,229.8 | 0 of 60 / 0 of 39 |\n\nThe mean full pipeline per subject is 19.12 min.\n\n**The problem:** the `Detection` column, and `Localization` with it, looks like a running total across subjects rather than a time per subject:\n- **It follows run order.** Sorted by value, the subjects come out in alphabetical order, with groupon and mozilla run last. Only 1 of 59 consecutive steps goes down; each crawl column has 27–30 drops.\n- **It doesn't track page size.** Correlation with run order is 0.956; with control count it's 0.05.\n- **The differences between consecutive values do track page size.** Correlation with node count is 0.70, and the biggest steps are the biggest pages: bowiestate 263 ms, canon 173 ms, cnn 161 ms.\n\nIf I'm right, the true detection-only cost is about **0.5 ms per control** pooled (0.51 on the 39 scored subjects; median 10 ms per subject). The 25.7 ms is about 50 times too high.\n\nThat changes what the brief asks me to write. If I publish \"detection only = 25.7 ms, clearly labelled\", I'd be repeating a second error. `FEASIBILITY.md`'s \"Detection averages 995 ms\" has the same problem. The full-pipeline figure is barely affected (about 1 s per subject), so every full-pipeline conclusion still holds: 0 of 60 under 300 ms, and it is the number to compare with Axcess's.\n\n**Decision needed:**\n1. **Go ahead as briefed, full pipeline as the headline.** I keep 25.7 as the detection-only figure but add a caveat that the column appears cumulative, and log it in §8.4.\n2. **Use the differenced figure (about 0.5 ms) for detection only**, with this evidence as a §8.4 entry. This changes the detection-only \"N of M faster\" count a lot.\n3. **Drop the detection-only figure** and state only the full-pipeline cost, plus a note that their `Detection` column can't be read as a per-subject time.\n\nI'd pick 2 or 3. The KAFE source isn't in `artifacts/`, so I can't confirm the running-total reading from their code; the evidence is statistical only.\n\nNothing is edited, regenerated or committed. `derived/kafe_matrix.jsonl` still has 52 lines. The only file I created is `COST-FIX-PROGRESS.md`; its step 3 records this stop and the evidence, so a new session can pick up from there.","ttft_ms":3508,"type":"result","duration_ms":116283,"uuid":"04b252cc-f83e-4d04-943c-c35b031ed7af","ttft_stream_ms":3295,"time_to_request_ms":136,"first_content_frame_ms":3295,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
